============================================================

Every major product area should have a stable route.

Examples:

/dashboard
/workspace
/settings
/billing
/account
/ai
/projects


Route names must remain predictable.

Navigation must not depend on fragile component state.


============================================================
38. FRONTEND DEPLOYMENT ENVIRONMENT
============================================================

Production frontend:

AWS Amplify

Backend:

https://api.zyrionos.com


Frontend must communicate through the production API configuration.

Environment-specific values belong in environment variables.


============================================================
39. OBSERVABILITY
============================================================

Important API operations should be traceable.

Development logging may include:

request
response status
operation duration
error category


Never log:

passwords
tokens
cookies
private API keys
payment secrets


============================================================
40. PERFORMANCE
============================================================

Frontend must avoid unnecessary API calls.

Examples:

Do not repeatedly fetch projects
because of uncontrolled rendering.

Do not call deployment endpoint multiple times
from a single click.

Do not reload entire application for small state changes.


Use targeted refreshes.


============================================================
41. CONSISTENCY RULE
============================================================

Every API-connected page must follow the same lifecycle:

IDLE
 ↓
LOADING
 ↓
SUCCESS

or

IDLE
 ↓
LOADING
 ↓
ERROR


For mutation:

READY
 ↓
SUBMITTING
 ↓
SUCCESS / ERROR


No page may invent its own contradictory lifecycle.


============================================================
42. API CONTRACT SOURCE OF TRUTH
============================================================

Backend route/controller/service definitions are authoritative.

Frontend documentation must match backend reality.

If backend changes:

API contract must be updated.

If frontend requires a new operation:

backend endpoint must be defined before UI
pretends that operation exists.


============================================================
43. NO FAKE FUNCTIONALITY RULE
============================================================

The following are prohibited:

fake deployment
fake payment success
fake project files
fake subscription
fake AI generation
fake live URLs
fake database records
fake success messages


UI may use visual placeholders during design phase,
but production functionality must use real data.


